1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:02,360
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:05,370
Darts!

3
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:08,100
You were expecting someone else?

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:11,379
Look, I want my company
back, so can the small talk.

5
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:14,780
As for me, I want your souls for my wall.

6
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:18,180
Then let's stop talking and
start dueling! Not alone.

7
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,740
This lunatic is far too dangerous.

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,629
So why don't you join him?

9
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:26,257
And when I defeat you, I'll get
two souls for the price of one!

10
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:30,260
Behold, a power that has
existed since the dawn of time.

11
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:34,760
Arise, Orychalcos Gaius!

12
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,860
Go, Master of Dragon Soldier!

13
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,260
What's going on?

14
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,640
What's that?

15
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:49,000
You're getting a glimpse of the legendary
city of Atlantis when I ruled as king!

16
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,280
You were king?

17
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,140
Indeed, I was.

18
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,997
And I shall be once again.

19
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:57,280
For when I defeat you,
paradise shall return!

20
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,340
It's time to

21
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:09,080
Behold, the lost city of Atlantis in all
its glory, just as it was 10,000 years ago.

22
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,560
A perfect civilization, or so I thought.

23
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:16,342
Surrounded by ocean, as
far as the eye could see,

24
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,108
we were isolated from
the rest of the world.

25
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,260
Our lives were simple.

26
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,220
We existed side by side with
all of Earth's creatures.

27
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:34,580
And we knew nothing of violence.

28
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:36,720
But then, that changed.

29
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:42,560
Darkness descended upon us.

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,540
And a strange substance
rained down from the heavens.

31
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:54,220
A substance that would change our lives.

32
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:56,420
The Orycalcus.

33
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,894
Please tell me that story time is over.

34
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,180
I'd like to duel.

35
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:05,320
The tale of my past directly
affects the fate of your future.

36
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,820
So if I were you, I'd pay close attention.

37
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:10,770
Now,

38
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:13,135
thanks to the stones of the Orycalcus,

39
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,437
the people of Atlantis
made advancements in

40
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,737
technology that were
never before imagined.

41
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:19,160
And soon,

42
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:24,720
I ruled over the most highly developed
civilization the world had ever known.

43
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:29,960
However, with progress comes
greed and eventually violence.

44
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,300
I knew what had to be done, but my father,

45
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,740
former King Ironheart,
had different ideas.

46
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,560
Ironheart was your father? But how?

47
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:43,600
If you ask questions, this
ridiculous story's never gonna end.

48
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:47,260
That old fool never had
what it took to be king.

49
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:54,120
And on my 21st birthday, he allowed me to
take over and fill his unimpressive shoes.

50
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:57,140
So as technology continued to advance,

51
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:01,597
and the hearts of my people continued
to sink deeper into the darkness,

52
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:04,220
it was up to me to remedy the situation.

53
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:07,877
The citizens of Atlantis were
growing more and more selfish,

54
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,737
and if I didn't act soon, I
would lose complete control.

55
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:14,173
But even I couldn't have
imagined what would happen next.

56
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:19,761
The Aurichalcos began to test us.

57
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,780
It revealed the truth about who we were.

58
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:32,500
Those who were wicked on the inside
became wicked on the outside.

59
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,532
Iona, are you all right?

60
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,760
Wait! Come back!

61
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,280
What's going on?

62
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,390
Iona!

63
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:58,760
I didn't realize it at first,

64
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:02,547
but the true colors of my people
were revealed to me that day.

65
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,240
But why?

66
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,200
Why is this happening?

67
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:18,620
I couldn't understand how a society as
perfect as ours could crumble like this.

68
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:26,900
But soon the Orichalcos would
answer all my questions.

69
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:30,217
The people of Atlantis were evil,

70
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:34,460
and I had been chosen to wipe
them out and start over again.

71
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:48,100
But I couldn't accomplish
such a task on my own.

72
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:52,560
I was but one man, so the
Orychalcos gave me a gift.

73
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:56,400
Something powerful enough to
lead my fight against mankind.

74
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,997
For deep below the Earth's surface lurked

75
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,727
the most incredible
creature that ever lived.

76
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,540
The Great Leviathan.

77
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,700
And it was mine.

78
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,860
And shortly this great beast will
return to finish what it began.

79
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:20,880
I was ready to begin my task of
recreating civilization on Earth,

80
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:23,680
but one person stood in my way.

81
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:26,600
My son, you know what you have to do.

82
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:31,600
Destroy those Orakalko stones so we
can return to the life we once knew.

83
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:37,840
Do you honestly believe we can
go back to the way things were?

84
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,064
It's too late for that, Father.

85
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,070
But darts...

86
00:06:41,153 --> 00:06:43,905
The true nature of our
people has been exposed.

87
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:48,920
We now know that the citizens of this
planet are evil and must be destroyed. What?

88
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,374
You heard me, old man.

89
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:54,620
We should be thanking the
Orychalcos for showing us the truth,

90
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:57,352
not blaming it for the faults of mankind.

91
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:03,420
Father, this mysterious substance that
rained down from above has opened up my eyes.

92
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,720
Not only has it shown me
what's wrong with the world,

93
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,260
it's given me the tools to fix it.

94
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:15,360
For I now have the power to awaken a mighty
creature known as the Great Leviathan.

95
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:18,120
And by the power of the Orychalcos,

96
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:22,457
this beast will rise up from the depths
of the earth and fight by my side.

97
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:25,780
And when I'm through, I
shall rebuild civilization.

98
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,230
Darts!

99
00:07:36,313 --> 00:07:37,220
What's going on?

100
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:41,300
Meet my Orichalco soldiers.

101
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,600
Grandpa, I'm scared.

102
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,586
If you join my side, you
have nothing to fear.

103
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,160
If not, then farewell.

104
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,440
We'll never join you. Never.

105
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:53,241
Let's go, Chris.

106
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,800
Have it your way.

107
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:14,133
The time has come to cleanse
the world of its impurities.

108
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:18,000
So arise, my children, and
conquer the people of Earth.

109
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,700
And this planet shall be yours.

110
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,601
What are we going to do, Grandpa?

111
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:42,513
Your father is under the control of
an evil force, and he must be stopped.

112
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,120
The future of our planet depends on it.

113
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,010
Through there.

114
00:08:47,093 --> 00:08:47,923
Hurry!

115
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,400
What's this?

116
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:58,014
Why are those monsters carved in stone?

117
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,760
We've come here to ask for their help.

118
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:20,457
and so the battle of atlantis began you
see my father had opened up a gateway to

119
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:23,017
the dominion of the beasts and he used the

120
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,571
monsters within to form an army of his own

121
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,700
Tell me, what was the battle's outcome?

122
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:40,555
Neither side was victorious, and
Atlantis sunk to the bottom of the sea.

123
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:44,097
My father's monster army
was scattered around the

124
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:47,180
world and sealed away until
they'd be needed again.

125
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:52,197
The Leviathan was drained of
his power and also sealed away.

126
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:57,280
It's taken me 10,000 years to gather
the energy necessary to bring it back.

127
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:01,200
All that's left for me to do
is defeat you two in this duel.

128
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,677
Then your souls will awaken the great

129
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:07,140
Leviathan and my plan
will finally come to pass.

130
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,490
Hold on.

131
00:10:08,573 --> 00:10:10,000
We already defeated you.

132
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:14,637
Our Master of Dragon Soldier should have
wiped out the rest of your life points.

133
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:17,602
Perhaps it should have,
but I'm afraid it didn't.

134
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:20,397
Your pathetic attack
fell short of its target.

135
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,660
So this duel's still on.

136
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,920
Hey, check it out! They're back! Awesome!

137
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,460
Go, Seto!

138
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,060
No way!

139
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,555
You didn't lose one single life point!

140
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,525
Didn't I just tell you
your attack didn't work?

141
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:50,300
Thanks to the special ability of my
Cutora, My damage was reduced to zero.

142
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,900
That's crazy!

143
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:55,917
He dodged an attack by
their strongest monster.

144
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,140
And what's worse, it's his turn now!

145
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,100
Orycalcos Gygas, return!

146
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:02,980
I told you, Kaiba.

147
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:07,260
Each time his Gygas is destroyed,
it comes back even stronger.

148
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,380
Face it, you'll never defeat me.

149
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,320
The power of the Orycalcos
will swallow you both.

150
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,795
Now back to the duel.

151
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:21,580
Since my Giygas returned
to me, I can't draw a card.

152
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:24,760
But no matter, everything
I need is in my hand.

153
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:28,260
So I'll enhance the power
of the seal with this.

154
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:31,180
The magic of Orycalcos Deuteros!

155
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:40,480
What's going on?

156
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,760
Somehow he's made the seal
of Orycalcos stronger!

157
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:12,600
Gentlemen, welcome to the
second level of darkness.

158
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,040
The what?

159
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:19,240
I don't know how, but Dot just added
another layer to the seal of Ory Kalkos.

160
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:20,890
Right.

161
00:12:20,973 --> 00:12:22,177
So what does that mean?

162
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:26,477
The first benefit of my Ory
Kalkos Duteros is the addition of

163
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:30,760
500 life points each turn for
every monster I have on the field.

164
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:34,820
Therefore, since I have two,
that's 1,000 points. What?

165
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:38,140
How are we supposed to
wipe him out? You're not.

166
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,000
It makes me invincible.

167
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:43,437
Next I'll attack your
master of dragons, soldier.

168
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:47,160
Go, my Ori-Kalcos Giygas!

169
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:51,520
Nice try, but my dragon's too strong!

170
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,940
You Tora!

171
00:12:58,260 --> 00:12:59,740
Absorb all the damage!

172
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:07,200
My life points are safe,
and now my Giygas returns!

173
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:14,960
That Kree, he's letting Azorichalcos
Gygus get its butt kicked on purpose,

174
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,926
so it can come back stronger.

175
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,620
That can't be it.

176
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:20,917
His monster would have
to be destroyed seven

177
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,437
more times before it
could defeat my dragon.

178
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:25,880
So there must be more to his plan.

179
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:31,620
Perhaps the secret lies in his cutora
and its ability to absorb attack damage.

180
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:36,080
Yes, that creature must have
another special ability.

181
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:39,320
All right, darts, my move!

182
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:42,620
As long as that eyesore is on the field,

183
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:45,397
it's pointless to attack
Izzoricalco's Giygas,

184
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,892
because darts won't lose any life points.

185
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,671
Plus, Giygas will just come back stronger.

186
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:55,140
But if I attack darts directly,
I should be able to win the duel!

187
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:59,300
I place one card face down on the field!

188
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:03,740
And next, I summon my Blade Knight!

189
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:11,420
And since I have only
one card left in my hand,

190
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:14,328
Blade Knight gets another
400 attack points.

191
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:19,680
I think that'll do for now.

192
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:22,375
He's setting himself up for something.

193
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:25,036
Yugi better not screw this up for me.

194
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,600
Time to pick up where I left off!

195
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:28,900
Yugi, hold on!

196
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:33,480
I'm sacrificing my Blade
Knight to activate this card!

197
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,540
Reflect energy!

198
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,480
All right, Yu-Gi,

199
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:46,739
it's up to you to blow this freak
show away with your Dragon Soldier.

200
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:47,920
Once you attack,

201
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,917
my Reflect Energy
Satellite will redirect the

202
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,540
blast to his light
points and wipe him out.

203
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:54,960
All right.

204
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:59,820
Dragon Soldier, attack
with Dragon Saber Blast!

205
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,550
Nice!

206
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:11,486
They were able to flatten
that freak together!

207
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:12,980
Of course they were!

208
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:16,240
Oh no!

209
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:20,060
That attack was supposed to
hit darts, not his monster!

210
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,900
It's a force field!

211
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,780
But how did he create it?

212
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:30,160
By using the second layer
of the seal, of course.

213
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:36,700
Whenever my life points are targeted, my
Oricalcos Deutero steps in to defend me.

214
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,030
It's simple.

215
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:41,960
I make a sacrifice so that
your monster takes the hit.

216
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,660
You know what that means, right?

217
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:47,700
Your dragon just attacked itself.

218
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,620
Pharaoh! Do something!

219
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:57,600
I activate my diffusion!

220
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,060
Talk about luck of the draw.

221
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,420
It's not luck.

222
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:08,717
It's through teamwork and determination
that we have avoided your attacks.

223
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:12,277
You have a little speech for
everything, don't you, Pharaoh?

224
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:15,700
You must get so tired of
being right all the time.

225
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,837
Well, don't worry, because
that all ends here.

226
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:22,680
So listen closely as I teach
you a little lesson of my own.

227
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:27,077
And I assure you, it has nothing
to do with teamwork or friendship.

228
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:32,860
And it all starts with this, a magic
card known as Orichalcos Mirror.

229
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:36,277
Now all I have to do is
sacrifice a monster from

230
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:39,700
my hand in order to summon
my Mirror Knight Calling,

231
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:43,860
which in turn calls four knights
to the field to protect me.

232
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,620
He played four monsters in one turn?

233
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,500
You poor fools.

234
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:54,311
You'll never get passed by Mirror Knights.

235
00:16:54,840 --> 00:17:01,640
And thanks to my Oricalcos Deuteros, I
gained 3,000 more life points. That's insane.

236
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:05,020
Now, pay close attention
to the mirror's reflection.

237
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,320
All right, what's going on?

238
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:12,217
Each knight reflects something or
someone on your side of the field.

239
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:15,320
That dictates the value
of their attack points.

240
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:16,897
So that means...

241
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:17,920
Yes, it does.

242
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:22,260
My knights receive the same number
of attack points as their target.

243
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:38,710
What's wrong?

244
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,824
Scared of your own reflections?

245
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:48,257
As long as my Mirror Knight
Calling Crystal is on the field,

246
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,693
my monster's shields will always return.

247
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:54,100
Which means my Mirror
Knights can't be destroyed.

248
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:57,089
So go ahead and summon
whatever you'd like.

249
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,160
Fine, I will.

250
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:02,920
But first, I think I'll
activate my card of Demise.

251
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:08,657
This lets me draw five new cards, as long
as I discard my entire hand in five turns.

252
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,580
But it's worth it, for a fresh start.

253
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:15,680
Next I'll play my Silent Doom card,

254
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:19,177
so I can summon a monster
from my grave in defense mode.

255
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:21,500
And I choose Blade Knight!

256
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:28,360
And now, I sacrifice Blade Knight
in order to summon Kaiser Glider!

257
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:32,160
And last, I'll place one card face down.

258
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,760
I must say, I'm impressed.

259
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:40,257
Your Kaiser Glider is safe from any monster
with the same number of attack points.

260
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:42,580
So my knights can't crush it.

261
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,040
Kaiba may be safe for now,

262
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:49,378
but we need to find a way to destroy
his monsters, not hide from them.

263
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,920
Alright, darts, my move.

264
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:57,080
Mirror Force, this should help.

265
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:00,340
First I'll place one card face down,

266
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:04,795
and then I'll summon my big shield
Gardner to the field in defense mode.

267
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,218
That's all for now.

268
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,660
How pathetic. Now then,

269
00:19:09,040 --> 00:19:14,640
since it's the start of a new turn for
me, I gain another 3,000 life points.

270
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,600
We must stop him and fast.

271
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:19,060
When Darts attacks,

272
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:24,066
I'll activate my mirror force to counteract
his mirrors and destroy his knights.

273
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:25,600
Hold on, folks.

274
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:27,840
I activate my trap card.

275
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:33,740
Your knights are only safe if your mirror
knight calling magic card is in play.

276
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:38,540
So now, I'll squash it
with Ring of Destruction.

277
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:52,700
Now, when your knights are
destroyed, they can't come back!

278
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:00,680
Hey, wait!

279
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:02,260
What's going on?

280
00:20:05,740 --> 00:20:06,880
Recognize anyone?

281
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:09,097
Yugi! But how?

282
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:12,800
I control the souls of
your companions, remember?

283
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,240
Let them go!

284
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:19,055
Attack my knights and you'll
be attacking your friends.

285
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:22,540
If I had played my mirror force,

286
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:27,720
that would mean my friends would
be gone forever by my own hand.

287
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,300
No matter what you do, you lose.

288
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:34,697
It's impossible to defeat me
without destroying these monsters.

289
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:40,160
And you can't destroy my knights without
destroying the souls of your friends.
